          {
            "title": "Order",
            "id": 129296,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>L'ordine delle istruzioni è importante. Una volta raccolto l'input e memorizzato in una variabile, possiamo riutilizzarlo.</p><p>Metti le righe nell'ordine corretto per usare l'output raccolto nell'istruzione di output.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"name_input = input()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi, \" /><text value=\"{name_input}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"75\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"What's your name?\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hi, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>name_input = input()</code>, seguito da <code>print(f\"Hi, {name_input}!\")</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>L'ordine delle istruzioni è importante. Usa <code>input()</code> per raccogliere una risposta, poi salvala in una variabile per riutilizzarla.</p><p>Ordina le righe per chiedere <code>What's your name?</code>, memorizzare la risposta e poi salutare l'utente.</p><p>Per l'input <code>Mimo</code>, stampa <code>Hi, Mimo!</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"name_input = input()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi, \" /><text value=\"{name_input}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"26\" /><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"75\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"input() = name_input\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print(f&quot;Hi, name_input!&quot;)\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"What's your name?\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hi, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>print(\"What's your name?\")</code>, seguito da <code>name_input = input()</code> e infine <code>print(f\"Hi, {name_input}!\")</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Console",
            "id": 129297,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per raccogliere l'input di un utente in un programma Python, usiamo la funzione <code>input</code>. L'input dell'utente può quindi essere assegnato a una variabile.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input()\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>input</code>, seguito da <code>(</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Per raccogliere l'input di un utente in un programma Python, usiamo la funzione <code>input</code>. L'input dell'utente può quindi essere assegnato a una variabile.</p><p>Memorizza una risposta dell'utente in <code>user_input</code>, senza stamparla ancora.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input()\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"10\" /><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"12\" /><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"output\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>user_input</code>, seguito da <code>=</code>, <code>input</code>, <code>(</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Displaying multiple times",
            "id": 129298,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Dopo aver acquisito l'input, possiamo assegnarlo a una variabile e usarlo proprio come qualsiasi altra variabile.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"user_input = input()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi, \" /><text value=\"{user_input}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"37\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"What's your name?\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hi, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>user_input</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Chiedi <code>What's your name?</code>, memorizza la risposta e usala in modo che l'input <code>Mimo</code> faccia stampare <code>Hi, Mimo!</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"user_input = input()\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(\" /><text value=\"f&quot;Hi, \" /><text value=\"{user_input}\" class=\"subst\" /><text value=\"!&quot;\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"name = input()\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"{name_input}\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;user_input&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"What's your name?\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Hi, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>user_input = input()</code>, seguito da <code>{user_input}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Prompt",
            "id": 129551,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Possiamo anche aggiungere un prompt aggiuntivo alla funzione <code>input</code>. Il prompt verrà visualizzato nella console.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"38\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Enter your name: \" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>\"Enter your name: \"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Possiamo anche aggiungere un prompt aggiuntivo alla funzione <code>input</code>. Il prompt verrà visualizzato nella console.</p><p>Completa la riga in modo che mostri esattamente il prompt <code>Enter your name: </code> e memorizzi ciò che l'utente digita in <code>user_input</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"13\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"38\" /><option startIndex=\"38\" endIndex=\"39\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"print\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&quot;What's your name?&quot;\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Enter your name: \" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Assicurati di scegliere <code>input</code>, seguito da <code>(</code>, <code>\"Enter your name: \"</code> e infine <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Output",
            "id": 129300,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Se inseriamo un prompt aggiuntivo, l'utente inizierà a digitare sulla stessa riga in cui il prompt viene visualizzato nella console.</p><p>Per questo è utile aggiungere uno spazio bianco alla fine del prompt usato nella funzione <code>input</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"user_input = input(\" /><text value=\"&quot;Enter your name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(f\" /><text value=\"&quot;Thanks, {user_input}!&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Enter your name: Mimo\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"Thanks, Mimo!\" /></content></output></code></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
